# What's New

<img width="700" alt="image" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/915480/91051685-156c4780-e63e-11ea-961e-bc90ca7fb131.png">

* Windows Desktop app automation - [Karate Robot](https://github.com/intuit/karate/tree/master/karate-robot) - also see the detailed [install guide](https://github.com/intuit/karate/wiki/Karate-Robot-Windows-Install-Guide)
* Revamped HTML report ([see video](https://twitter.com/KarateDSL/status/1237797240686522369))
* Intercept browser HTTP requests in Chrome ([see video](https://twitter.com/KarateDSL/status/1248996522357739521))
* [`configure callSingleCache`](https://github.com/intuit/karate#configure-callsinglecache) - so that you don't need to wait for a "sign-in flow", every time you re-run a test in dev mode
* [`driver.inputFile()`](https://github.com/intuit/karate/tree/master/karate-core#driverinputfile) - Chrome-native file-upload 
* WebDriver support for the new (Chromium based) Microsoft Edge browser
* Improved tree walking in UI tests, e.g. [`locateAll()`, `parent`, `children`](https://github.com/intuit/karate/tree/master/karate-core#tree-walking) etc.
* Multiple mock files can be combined into one at run-time (thanks @michaelpro1)
* [CLI testing support](https://twitter.com/maxandersen/status/1276431309276151814) ! See [this thread](https://stackoverflow.com/a/62911366/143475) for details
* `match` can finally be used in JS with all the power you normally have in feature files, see [this thread](https://github.com/intuit/karate/issues/1202) and some extras to introspect object / data types within JS blocks
* [`contains deep`](https://github.com/intuit/karate#match-contains-deep) for recursive nested JSON matching ([see example](https://twitter.com/KarateDSL/status/1287658286657855490))

<img width="700" alt="image" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/915480/91042010-ac310800-e62e-11ea-9b18-bf8fc2736889.png">

# Breaking Changes
* `match contains` will *not* recurse nested items [any more](https://github.com/intuit/karate/issues/1289), use `contains deep` as explained above
* [`karate.stop()`](https://github.com/intuit/karate#karate-stop) now takes a mandatory port number argument, so you can call the same (static) `cURL` command to resume, e.g. `curl localhost:8080`
* [`exists()`](https://github.com/intuit/karate/tree/master/karate-core#exists) API refactored for UI tests, see [this thread](https://github.com/intuit/karate/issues/1148) for details
* a `match` with a primitive number on the right-hand-side could incorrectly pass, this should be very rare - see [this thread](https://github.com/intuit/karate/issues/1179#issuecomment-646121572) for details
* again extremely unlikely and rare, but a backslash (`\`) character was getting swallowed in doc-string (triple-quote) sections, so in case you were escaping them, you don't need to any more ([commit details](https://github.com/intuit/karate/commit/d37f87b066471254cb5280fd64afc1f26f0b8235))

For a list of all issues closed in this release, go [here](https://github.com/intuit/karate/milestone/16?closed=1).

